From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:16:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: use the right CCA control register on
 mt7916/mt798x

mt7915_mac_cca_stats_reset() always used the mt7915 address layout for
MT_WF_PHY_RX_CTRL1, while mt7915_mac_enable_nf() already picks the
mt7916 layout (band stride 1 << 20) for the same register on the other
chips. On band 1 of mt7916/mt798x it therefore set bits in an unrelated
register in band 0's PHY space on every channel change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mac.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index 27d768a3..c3054e0c 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -1096,7 +1096,9 @@ void mt7915_queue_rx_skb(struct mt76_dev *mdev, enum mt76_rxq_id q,
 void mt7915_mac_cca_stats_reset(struct mt7915_phy *phy)
 {
 	struct mt7915_dev *dev = phy->dev;
-	u32 reg = MT_WF_PHY_RX_CTRL1(phy->mt76->band_idx);
+	u8 band = phy->mt76->band_idx;
+	u32 reg = is_mt7915(&dev->mt76) ? MT_WF_PHY_RX_CTRL1(band) :
+					  MT_WF_PHY_RX_CTRL1_MT7916(band);
 
 	mt76_clear(dev, reg, MT_WF_PHY_RX_CTRL1_STSCNT_EN);
 	mt76_set(dev, reg, BIT(11) | BIT(9));
